course: dictionary
lesson: 3171
title: Words with two meanings: employ
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and employ is one of them. Its first meaning is to give someone a job and pay them. «Self-employed people work for themselves» means nobody gives them a job or pays them wages, so they earn from their own work.
explain: Its second meaning is more formal: to use something, usually a method or a plan. In an exam, «employ a suitable method» means use a sensible way to solve the problem. To check which meaning fits, swap in use or give a job to and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The words around employ give you clues. «When someone is too ill to work they call in sick» and «some employers keep paying them» tell you that employers are the people who give work and pay wages. Employed workers are paid by an employer; self-employed people are paid by their own work.
fact: Employ (verb) means to give someone a job and pay them.
fact: Employers are the people or companies who give work and pay wages.
fact: «Self-employed» people work for themselves, so they must work out and pay their own tax.
fact: Self-employed people get no sick pay or holiday pay, but an employed worker often does.
fact: In formal writing, employ can mean to use something, as in «employ a strategy».
exercise: «Self-employed people work for themselves.» Who pays a self-employed person? | Their employer pays them each week | *They earn from their own work | Their school pays them | A bank pays them every hour
exercise: «The company decided to employ twenty new workers.» What does employ mean here? | To use twenty tools | To hide twenty people | *To give twenty people a job and pay them | To teach twenty children
exercise: «The team had to employ a clever strategy to win.» What does employ mean here? | Forget | Give a job to | *Use | Break
test: «Some employers keep paying a worker who is off sick.» Who are employers? | Children at school | People who make clothes | *People who give others jobs and pay them | People who ride bicycles
test: Which sentence uses employ to mean use? | He is employed by the city council | The farm employs many workers | The shop will employ five new staff | *She will employ a clever method to solve it
exam: Which is true of a self-employed worker? | They get sick pay from a boss | *They work for themselves and pay their own tax | They are always paid by the government | They never do any work at all
